/*
   Strategy
   --------
   This metamodel describes JavaScript source syntax for the purpose of
   emission. It is plain ECMAScript: no type annotations, no interfaces,
   no type aliases, no generics — every construct has a runtime meaning.
   (Type syntax is stripped by esbuild before execution anyway, so the
   model carries only what runs.)

   Scope
   -----
   A deliberately small surface: enough JavaScript to express light
   implementations (functions, classes, statements, expressions,
   destructuring, template literals). Grown demand-driven, one node at a
   time, as real emitters need new forms.

   Modeling notes
   --------------
   - `Node` is the root marker, mirroring ts.Node. Statement and Expression
     live in metamodel_code.pure; declarations that are also statements live
     in metamodel_structure.pure.
   - `Identifier` is a single class with a `text` slot, not a bare string,
     leaving room for attaching source position / import source later.
   - Modifiers are a flat enum (`ModifierFlag`) carried as a list. Only the
     JS-meaningful flags survive: Static, Async, Export, Default.
   - Bodies are modelled as `Block[0..1]` so empty-body forms are
     first-class. Arrow-function concise bodies are a separate slot
     (`expressionBody`).
*/

import meta::external::language::javascript::metamodel::*;

// =============================================================================
// Node — root of the syntax tree. Marker base; mirrors ts.Node.
// =============================================================================

Class meta::external::language::javascript::metamodel::Node
{
}
